It flies pretty far too! Hey you should definitely teach it on your channel

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:19.980
And is pretty sharp too! I'm sure they're
going to like it! The triple ninja star

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.290
or ninja tri-star

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:24.520
is a type of modular Origami, meaning
we're going to interlock

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.420
each of these individual units together in
order to get the ninja star

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.880
if you're going to use Origami paper,
make sure that the white side is facing

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.100
up like this when you start. I'm using
three colored sheets

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.240
of letter size paper. To make it into a
square I take the top edge and fold it

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.520
down to the left side

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:47.520
and then I tear it along this edge here.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.410
Now that we have a fold going this way
we're going to take the upper left

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:55.870
corner and fold it down to the lower
right corner

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:59.290
line up the edges..

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:06.290
and then make a crease along the edge

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.190
now you'll see we have an X in the paper

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.540
once again just fold it on the diagonal
and we're going to take this lower edge

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.100
here

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.940
and we're going to take both these
layers and fold them

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.490
up to this edge, so you can just kinda
hold it like this

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:29.150
and line this edge up at the top

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:35.230
once everything's lined up then you can
make a crease. Now

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:38.319
you'll see we have a big triangle here
on the left and a

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:41.849
right triangle over here on the right
we're going to take this

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:45.230
edge of the smaller triangle and we're
going to fold it up

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.690
so that it meets this edge which we just
folded in right here

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.660
so you can just take it like this it's
probably easier to set it down

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:58.989
but just so you could see, fold it up
like that

00:02:58.989 --> 00:03:02.290
line up the edges

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:07.420
and then crease it

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.769
Now, we're going to flip the model
around

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:14.950
and I'm going to take a this edge here

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:19.150
that we just made and I'm gonna fold
it up to the top edge right here

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.540
So take it

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.210
fold it up

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.310
and you could hold it right here,

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.900
make sure the edges all lined up

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.920
and then you can make that crease

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.180
If you're using printer, it's going to get thick here, so just be sure to hold it

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.200
it nice and tight

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.870
when your folding it. Once again we're
going to take

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.130
this bottom edge and fold it up to the
top

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:51.870
here it gets a little bit thick so be
sure to hold it snug right here

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.190
with your right hand. Now you can fold it up
you'll see this corner right here

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:00.800
will actually join with this corner
that's right here

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.459
Just fold it

00:04:05.459 --> 00:04:09.110
join those corners up, pinch it..

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:15.980
and make crease along the bottom

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.500
It's a little thick, but just crease it as best
you can

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.000
Now, you can actually

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.640
unfold this corner by grabbing this
corner here

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.780
and just pull it out just like that

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:34.479
and this corner which is tucked in, you
could just unfold this as well

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:40.630
So your paper should look something like
this:

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.840
now we're going to fold this

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.169
edge right here along this

00:04:47.169 --> 00:04:50.169
crease which we made, so you just want to fold

00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:55.840
on that crease right here

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.750
just like that

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.729
we're going to take this corner and
we're going to fold it in

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:07.479
by taking this edge and aligning it

00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:11.840
with this edge if the paper so it's easier
if you can hold it like this

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:15.490
Then you can easily take that edge 

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.400
hold this down with your left hand so it's
nice and flush with the paper

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.750
and make sure

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:26.430
that edge lines up with the other edge

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:31.160
then you can make that crease there. Okay so
now that this corners folded in

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.180
we're going to take this edge in the
paper here

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.520
and we're going to join it with this
edges as well

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:42.349
So, what you do.. fold that in like that

00:05:42.349 --> 00:05:47.080
and you could just pinch it like this

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:50.349
now as you'll see on the paper

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:55.050
there actually is a crease that goes
diagonally like this

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:58.910
however we need to make a new crease
right next to it

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:03.199
where this corner meets the paper we
need to make a mark

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:09.860
Right there. Now if you want to be really
precise and you're using

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.479
eight-and-a-half by 11 paper

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:15.800
the mark that you're going to make is
exactly five millimeters (half a

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:16.590
centimeter)

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:20.560
to the left on the bottom up this crease
right there

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.099
if you follow this little crease all the
way to the top

00:06:24.099 --> 00:06:27.610
right at the top here is where we're
going to make the second mark

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:32.080
now I'm going to draw a line so that you
could see it a little easier

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.979
so as you'll see it's just a little bit
off

00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:40.110
from the main mark and the reason that
we're doing this

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:43.210
is because this angle that we're going
to make has to be

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:46.300
a 120 degrees now we're going to take

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.310
this bottom edge and we're going to fold
it up

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:54.599
so that it lies directly on that line we
just drew

00:06:54.599 --> 00:06:57.930
put your finger nail right here in the
corner and pull up

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.990
now you can lay that edge directly on
that line

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:05.500
all the way to the top just like that

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:08.210
and make crease along the bottom here

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.740
So you should have something that looks
just like this

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.630
Now, you can unfold this

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:19.349
and just flatten it out. We're going
to take

00:07:19.349 --> 00:07:23.020
this part of the paper and we're going
to fold directly on

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:27.289
this crease here right where my finger
is when you take this paper

00:07:27.289 --> 00:07:34.289
and we're going to fold up like this 

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:40.500
And we're going to take the rest of this paper here

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:46.210
and we're going to wrap it around just like
this

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:51.270
Pull it nice and tight!

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:57.030
it's not gonna quite line up at the
bottom here but that's okay

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:01.000
now you'll see we have a little flap
here

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.830
and we have a pocket right in here you
want to take this flap

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:09.940
and you're going to fold it down so that

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:15.099
the fold lines up with the top of the
pocket just like that

00:08:15.099 --> 00:08:21.250
now you can open the pocket and you can
tuck this flap in

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:26.819
as far as it can go

00:08:26.819 --> 00:08:31.360
just like that. There you go!

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:35.190
that's how to make the modular
3-Point Tri-Star Unit!

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:38.539
once you've made three then we can interlock them

00:08:38.539 --> 00:08:42.490
if you take a look at the unit you'll
notice there's a pocket here on the front

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.790
where we tucked that flap

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.180
there's a pocket on the back on the same
side

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:52.020
it's a little bit thinner and there's also
a point here

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:55.310
we're going to flip all three units

00:08:55.310 --> 00:09:00.899
upside down so that thinner pocket
is on the top

00:09:00.899 --> 00:09:05.459
then we could take two of the units
we're going to take this point

00:09:05.459 --> 00:09:08.570
that doesn't have the pocket and

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:12.140
we're going to join it with the thin
pocket here

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:17.410
that doesn't have that little flap, so
you're gonna take two pieces like this

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:22.209
take the point and put it
right in the pocket just like that

00:09:22.209 --> 00:09:26.880
and just use your thumb to kind of push
it down.. now we're going to take the

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:27.490
other one

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:31.070
and just remember we're holding it so
that the pocket

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:35.190
where the flap was tucked in is on the back
again

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:38.399
we're going to take this point and we're
going to put it

00:09:38.399 --> 00:09:44.709
into the thin pocket right here on this
piece now

00:09:44.709 --> 00:09:46.160
and slide at all the way in

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.610
we're going to take this third piece
that we just tucked in

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:52.860
and we're going to take this part with
the pockets

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.920
and we're going to put it underneath the
tip

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.939
of the first one the blue one, so take
it

00:09:59.939 --> 00:10:03.610
and slide that underneath like that
you'll see

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:06.850
this is the point of the blue piece

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:11.529
we're gonna bend it and put it in this
little sleeve or pocket

00:10:11.529 --> 00:10:16.489
of the yellow piece, which is the third
piece, so all you need to do is to round

00:10:16.489 --> 00:10:17.660
this off a little bit

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:21.540
put that inside

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:26.799
all the way in and use your thumb to
kind of push it

00:10:26.799 --> 00:10:29.929
Then you can set it down

00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:33.089
flatten everything out and there you go!

00:10:33.089 --> 00:10:36.549
You have the Triple Ninja Star..now as
you'll notice

00:10:36.549 --> 00:10:40.540
is a little bit concave meaning these
points are actually bent

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:44.100
a little bit to the left like that when
you see these tabs

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:47.980
on the right. If you didn't make the
guide Mark correctly or you folded it at

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.279
the existing crease

00:10:49.279 --> 00:10:54.309
this is what would happen. Now I'll show you how to throw it. Alright so I found that

00:10:54.309 --> 00:10:55.149
the best way to

00:10:55.149 --> 00:10:58.499
to throw it is to have these little tabs
on the back

00:10:58.499 --> 00:11:02.589
facing to the right, so you can hold it
just like this

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:06.059
in your right hand. If you're lefty,
you can throw it like this

00:11:06.059 --> 00:11:09.529
Hold it like this and throw it

00:11:09.529 --> 00:11:15.430
overhand and let it spin out of your hand

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.870
If you want to try to throw it sideways you
can do that as well

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.440
Let's see if I can hit my portrait

